<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><a href="https://www.relay.fm/intentional/6">On this episode of <em>Intentional AI</em></a>, Chris and I get into my email odyssey, the months I spent trying to hand my email over to a robot. First came the Big Swing, where I would never open email again and the robot read everything and handed me a table, which burned tokens and did not survive two weeks. What actually works is a lot less glamorous, where I do the triage myself in Superhuman and the robot sweeps up behind me, moving newsletters into Readwise Reader and logging purchases and sponsor deals into Obsidian.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">I also walk through my customer support robot. Chris shares his own experiment of an hour of meditation a day before his first baby arrives, and we close with the Gemini Notebook rebrand, Claude Opus 5, and Siri AI finding Chris an airport lounge at O&#8217;Hare.</p>
